Phase 1 – Level 3 puzzles
Step L3-1 – Level 3 skeleton
Goal: Level 3 exists with three empty rooms, a new palette, a camera that follows vertically, and shows up in both room selects.
Test: you can pick 3A, 3B or 3C from the main menu and the pause menu, spawn on the right floor, and the camera follows up and down without jerking. Levels 1 and 2 still work.


Step L3-2 – Timed switch, fold sheet and room 3A
Goal: the first Hard room: a timed action far from where it pays off, and wind that only works after a fold.
Test: the fan does nothing useful while the sheet is closed. Pressing the switch opens the sheet and the draught reaches full height. The timer is clearly visible. If the timer ends while you are in the sheet, it waits and doesn't crush you. The ledge can't be reached by jumping.

Step L3-3 – Fold bridge, seal links and room 3B
Goal: form change, then the sword, then a forced crossing.
Test: you can't pass the slit standing, you can't cut the seal while flat, cutting it unfolds the bridge segment by segment, and the pit under the gap is shallow enough to jump out of. Without the bridge the gap can't be crossed.

Step L3-4 – Room 3C
Goal: the finale puzzle, all three mechanics in one sequence.
Test: after dropping in you must pass the slit, cut the seal, and then the sheet opens and the draught reaches the platform. Reset after the drop returns you to the second checkpoint, not to 3B. You can't reach the platform any other way.

Step L3-5 – Recorded solutions for Level 3
Goal: proof that every Level 3 room can be solved without enemies.

Phase 2 – The snake and placing enemies 

Step L3-6 – The snake
Goal: an enemy that is fast and dangerous, but that you can always read and answer.
Test: every attack shows Rear and Mark first, the snake never appears on top of you, it ignores you while you are flat in a slit, two hits kill it, and the first hit makes it vanish hurt.

Step L3-7 – Place the enemies
Goal: the rooms play as designed, with enemies in them.
Test: each room is beatable, nothing feels unfair, and the bat in 3A and 3C bends in the draught.

Step L3-8 – Second crease choice
Test: the choice screen appears after Level 2, both new creases work, the earlier crease is kept, and no room needs any crease.

Step L3-9 – Stars and par times
Test: Room select shows 3 stars per room for all nine rooms, kept for the session, with best time and fewest resets.

Step L3-10 – The ending
Test: after the 3C exit door the sequence plays (about 12 seconds), can be skipped with Enter after 2 seconds, and ends on a Game complete screen with the right totals.
